Berserk — native desktop and browser clients for berserk-nxt

Original project: https://github.com/SkAZi/berserk-nxt
Original author: Игорь «SkAZi» Потапов
Source revision: bf754902127c84baf1a403b0b0bc02e1b1bf417d

The original project's LGPL-3.0 license is retained in LICENSE.
The Rust implementation adapts the upstream card schema, collection/deck formats,
compact deck encoding, squad rules, and Tabletop Simulator atlas
format. Bundled card data, constants, ratings and card images come from that source
revision. Card text and artwork retain their original credits and rights; the
software license does not imply ownership of the Berserk game or its artwork.

All application views, state management, storage integration and domain logic in
src/ are implemented in Rust using egui/eframe (desktop) and Leptos (browser). No Electron, Svelte or Node.js runtime
is required. Python is used by the data collection, validation and synchronization utilities.

